course: dictionary
lesson: 13592
title: Words that mean not important
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how much something matters. Inconsequential means not important, so small that it does not change much. Read the words around it to check. «The spelling mistake was inconsequential, so the teacher did not even mark it.» The teacher ignored the mistake, so it must be too small to matter.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. Then swap in your meaning. «The scratch on the desk was inconsequential.» If "unimportant" fits in that place and the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Scientists and mathematicians use the word too. «The tiny change in temperature was inconsequential, and the result stayed the same.» The change is so small that it makes no real difference to the answer.
fact: Inconsequential means not important; too small to matter.
fact: The word starts with in-, which means not. Consequential means important or having results, so inconsequential means the opposite.
fact: Phrases you may meet are inconsequential details and an inconsequential mistake.
fact: «An inconsequential remark» is a remark that does not matter to the story or the conversation.
fact: Unimportant is a close synonym, but inconsequential often suggests something so small that it can safely be ignored.
exercise: «The mistake in the title was inconsequential.» What does inconsequential mean? | Very important and serious | Loud and sudden | Hard to see clearly | *Not important, too small to matter
exercise: Which word could replace inconsequential in «an inconsequential remark»? | Huge | Angry | *Unimportant | Clever
exercise: Why might a scientist say a change was inconsequential? | It was the biggest change of all | *It was so small it made no real difference to the result | It made the experiment fail completely | It surprised everyone in the lab
test: «The wrinkle on his shirt was inconsequential; nobody noticed.» What does inconsequential mean here? | Very loud | Very dirty | *Not important | Brand new
test: Which word means the opposite of inconsequential? | *Important | Ordinary | Tiny | Quiet
exam: What does «an inconsequential remark» tell the reader about the remark? | It is the first thing the writer says | *It does not matter much | It is very rude and shouted | It is the longest sentence in the book
